🔄 CREATING AND CONNECTING CI/CD PIPELINE BETWEEN EC2 & GITHUB

Connect to EC2 Using Terminal

ssh -i mykey.pem ubuntu@<EC2_PUBLIC_IP>


(Replace <EC2_PUBLIC_IP> with your instance’s public IP)

Add GitHub Secrets (for CI/CD connection)

Go to GitHub → Repository → Settings → Secrets → Actions → New repository secret

Add the following secrets one by one:

EC2_SSH_PRIVATE_KEY → Paste private key from ~/.ssh/id_ed25519

EC2_HOST → Your EC2 public IP

EC2_USER → deploy

Alternative Way to Connect to EC2 (via AWS Console)

Go to AWS → EC2 → Instances

Select your instance

Click Connect

Choose EC2 Instance Connect (Browser-based SSH)

Click Connect to open terminal directly in your browser 
